      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree, that \"Direct PCM\" is QC specific feature, but AOSP supports DIRECT flags. I have seen in case of policymixes that direct paths should be preferred, if available (because the direct paths will avoid processing at FWK)\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp;l\u003d1267?q\u003d%22if%20a%20direct%20output%20can%20be%20opened%20to%20deliver%20the%20track%27s%20multi-channel%20content%20to%20the%22\n\nbased on these logics we are under impression that direct path should be tried first if not available then try for deep buffer (r/3206279) \n\n\nIf we try to play a multi channel clip with params 16bit, stereo, 192k and direct paths publish this support, but if we explicitly add deep_buffer check, (which APM added just before calling openDirectOutput), it won\u0027t allow a direct output.",
